---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro"
import Text from "@components/core/Text.astro"
import { Pages } from "@utils"
import PartnerFooter from "@components/PartnerFooter.astro"
---

<Layout title="Tennibot vs. Lobster | Tennibot" showFooter={false} showHeader={false} showPartnerHeader={true} showSecondaryHeader={false} showSecondaryMenu={false}>
    <main class="bg-t-off-black overflow-hidden text-t-off-white" >
        <section class="w-[80%] mx-auto mt-36 mb-24" >
            <Text tag="h1" className="font-avenirBold text-t-green text-center md:text-4xl text-2xl mb-10" >Tennibot Partner vs. Lobster: What You Need to Know</Text>
        </section>

        <section class="w-[80%] mx-auto" >
            <Text tag="h2" className="font-avenirBold text-t-green text-xl mb-10" >
                Not all ball machines are created equal.
            </Text>
            <Text tag="p" className="font-plutoLight text-t-off-white text-base mb-10" >
                If you're weighing the Tennibot Partner against a classic like the Lobster ball machine, here’s what you need to know before investing in your training.
            </Text>

            <Text tag="h3" className="font-avenirBold text-t-green text-xl mb-10" >
                1. Legacy vs. Intelligent Innovation
            </Text>
            <Text tag="p" className="font-plutoLight text-t-off-white text-base mb-10" >
                Lobster has earned its reputation with dependable, well-built machines that have served players for decades. Their Grand Five LE offers solid programmable features like 12 built-in drills, adjustable spin, and custom settings. It’s a trusted tool for traditional training. <br/><br/>But Tennibot isn’t just a ball machine—it’s a smart training ecosystem. The Partner leverages real-time AI, vision-guided shot delivery, and adaptive play powered by synchronized 4K cameras. The Partner dynamically adjusts speed, angle, and placement based on where you are on the court—something no static program can do.
            </Text>

            <Text tag="h3" className="font-avenirBold text-t-green text-xl mb-10" >
                2. Smart Mobility & Real-Court Simulation
            </Text>
            <Text tag="p" className="font-plutoLight text-t-off-white text-base mb-10" >
                Lobster models are wheeled and portable, but they stay in place once the session starts. <br/><br/>Tennibot Partner? It moves. Autonomously. Across the court. Delivering shots from multiple angles and positions to mimic real opponents. You’re not just hitting balls—you’re training with movement, reaction, and match-readiness built in.
            </Text>

            <Text tag="h3" className="font-avenirBold text-t-green text-xl mb-10" >
                3. Vision-Driven Intelligence vs. Blind Launching
            </Text>
            <Text tag="p" className="font-plutoLight text-t-off-white text-base mb-10" >
                Lobster machines don’t “see” the court. They don’t know where the player is, where the net is, or how the ball is interacting with the environment. No cameras, no real-time tracking, no adaptability. <br/><br/>Tennibot Partner is powered by a vision system built for elite-level training. It uses synchronized 4K cameras and proprietary algorithms to track court lines, player positioning, and lighting conditions—delivering consistent, intelligent drills that adapt to the way you play
            </Text>

            <Text tag="h3" className="font-avenirBold text-t-green text-xl mb-10" >
                4. Portable Power vs. Plug-in Limitations
            </Text>
            <Text tag="p" className="font-plutoLight text-t-off-white text-base mb-10" >
                Many Lobster machines rely on AC power or built-in lead-acid batteries that are heavy, slow to charge, and outdated by modern standards. <br /><br />Tennibot Partner uses swappable, tool-grade lithium batteries (Makita-compatible), offering rapid charging (60–90 minutes) and unlimited playtime with spare packs. You can train as long as you want—no extension cords or recharge breaks required.
            </Text>

            <Text tag="h3" className="font-avenirBold text-t-green text-xl mb-10" >
                5. Smarter Workflow, Simpler Experience
            </Text>
            <Text tag="p" className="font-plutoLight text-t-off-white text-base mb-10" >
                Adjusting drills on Lobster often involves knobs, remote controls, and trial-and-error setups. The machine has no context about the drill or the player—it just launches balls in a pre-set pattern. <br/><br />With Tennibot, you control everything from your phone. The mobile app lets you define shot patterns, intensity, and ball frequency with a few taps. Want to change drills mid-session? No problem—just tap and go.
            </Text>

            <Text tag="h3" className="font-avenirBold text-t-green text-xl mb-10" >
                Final Thoughts
            </Text>
            <Text tag="p" className="font-plutoLight text-t-off-white text-base mb-10" >
                The Lobster builds reliable, traditional, no-frills ball machines. But if you’re looking to level up with cutting-edge tech, full-court simulation, and a smart ecosystem that grows with you, <span class="font-avenirBold text-t-green" >Tennibot Partner is in a league of its own</span>.
            </Text>

            <Text tag="h3" className="font-avenirBold text-t-green text-xl mb-10" >
                This is more than a ball machine. This is the future of training.
            </Text>
        </section>
    </main>
</Layout>
<PartnerFooter />